---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Parsing Unstructured Orders Into Actionable Data - Marker">
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-24 md:pb-24">
      <a href="/case-studies" class="mb-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
        <svg class="mr-1 h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
        </svg>
        All Case Studies
      </a>

      <span class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Office & Business Supply Chain</span>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Parsing Unstructured Orders Into Actionable Data</h1>

      <div class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm">
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Company</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">National office supply retailer operating 50 fulfillment centers and 250 last-mile facilities</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Team</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Supply chain technology group managing all systems across retail operations</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Key Challenge</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Customer orders arriving as unstructured email requiring manual parsing, alongside system walls between OMS, WMS, and TMS</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Challenge</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The supply chain technology leader at this national office supply retailer — with 15 years of prior experience in fulfillment operations at a major big-box retailer — managed all supply chain systems across the business: order management, warehouse management, and transportation management. Each system had "walls" that data couldn't easily cross, despite standardization efforts.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">One particularly acute pain point was customer orders arriving as unstructured email. Business customers would send orders in free-form formats — sometimes as email body text, sometimes as attached spreadsheets with inconsistent column layouts. These required manual parsing before they could enter the order management system. The technology leader noted that while the emails were unstructured, each customer tended to follow their own recognizable pattern — a pattern a system could learn.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Between systems, field conversions added further friction. Data leaving the OMS needed to be reformatted before entering the TMS. These translations were manual, error-prone, and consumed engineering time that could be spent on higher-value projects.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Marker ingests unstructured email orders and learns each customer's communication patterns over time. As the system processes orders from the same customer, it builds a model of their formatting habits — column layouts, product naming conventions, quantity formats — and parses future orders with increasing accuracy. Exceptions are flagged for human review rather than requiring manual parsing of every order.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">For the system wall problem, Marker acts as a communication layer that sits between the OMS, WMS, and TMS, handling the field translations that currently require manual intervention. When an order moves from management to fulfillment to transportation, Marker ensures the data arrives in the format each downstream system expects — bridging the gaps that standardization alone hasn't closed.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-muted-foreground">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Unstructured email orders parsed automatically by learning each customer's communication patterns</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Exceptions flagged for human review rather than requiring manual parsing of every inbound order</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Field translations between OMS, WMS, and TMS handled automatically, bridging system walls</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Engineering time redirected from data plumbing to higher-value supply chain improvements</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">See how Marker turns unstructured communication into structured, actionable data.</p>
        <a href="/book-demo" class="mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2">Book a Demo</a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
